WEBVTT

00:00:02.229 --> 00:00:08.179
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the sixteenth. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:08.699 --> 00:00:17.100
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, you're there. Before we start, whose new car is that in the car park? Takes up most of the view from the window.</v>

00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:21.579
<v David Whitfield>Not mine. Mine's the one held together with road salt.</v>

00:00:22.649 --> 00:00:26.500
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Thought we'd had a visiting director. Very shiny for this place.</v>

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:29.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, vehicle inspection over. Everyone on?</v>

00:00:31.329 --> 00:00:37.280
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. Just heard someone mention the charity bake sale on Friday. Apparently my flapjack's still being discussed.</v>

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:43.520
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The charity bake sale on Friday, yeah. That flapjack needed a permit to break into.</v>

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:47.840
<v Hannah Price>It was structurally sound. I'll give it that.</v>

00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:53.789
<v Sarah Okafor>Unlike this conversation. Right, closed work first, then what's actually needed.</v>

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:02.640
<v Grace Liu>I signed off the inspection on the IM1 hydraulic unit on Tuesday. That's last Tuesday, obviously. All closed, not another inspection for today's list.</v>

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:08.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely, that was the old entry I was looking at.</v>

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:16.540
<v Sarah Okafor>And I tested the boiler safety valve yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done as well.</v>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.079
<v Hannah Price>Finished the repair on the water booster last night. That's complete from my side.</v>

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:30.439
<v David Whitfield>Ah, good. That was the one still showing on the old handover, wasn't it?</v>

00:01:32.239 --> 00:01:35.040
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, old information. Not asking for another repair.</v>

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:42.950
<v Tomasz Nowak>While we're on nights, noticed the CT1 was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:47.260
<v Grace Liu>Settled back to normal, you mean?</v>

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:52.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, normal again. Just an observation, not raising a job off it.</v>

00:01:54.590 --> 00:02:02.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Same sort of thing, I heard a slight rattle from the fire panel, nothing to action yet. Just saying what I heard.</v>

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:07.519
<v Grace Liu>Understood. No fault job being raised for that noise.</v>

00:02:09.389 --> 00:02:16.389
<v Grace Liu>Separately, we do still need someone to run a function test on the fire panel. No rush on that one.</v>

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:22.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take the function test? It's separate from the rattle, to be clear.</v>

00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:26.319
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not me, sorry. Haven't got room to take that on.</v>

00:02:28.219 --> 00:02:34.169
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, no takers. The fire panel function test stays unallocated, no rush. Nobody against it as owner.</v>

00:02:36.259 --> 00:02:42.560
<v David Whitfield>Yeah so, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the wrapper tomorrow. Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:48.740
<v Hannah Price>Is that the jam itself, or are you thinking the sensor's what's keeping it stopped?</v>

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:57.909
<v David Whitfield>Could be either at the minute. That's why I'm taking both together, rather than calling the sensor faulty before I've cleared it.</v>

00:03:00.169 --> 00:03:05.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Davey. Clear the jam and check the sensors on the wrapper tomorrow, fairly important. Agreed.</v>

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.069
<v David Whitfield>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:03:10.979 --> 00:03:17.280
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll investigate the pressure drop on the boiler feed pump tomorrow at 9:30. No rush on that one.</v>

00:03:19.729 --> 00:03:22.530
<v David Whitfield>You've got the pressure history already, haven't you?</v>

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:32.289
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I've got the existing trend in front of me. Enough to start the investigation; I'm not claiming we've found a cause yet.</v>

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Fiona, boiler feed pump pressure drop investigation tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:03:38.979 --> 00:03:42.479
<v Fiona Doyle>That's right. No rush, just keeping that time for it.</v>

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:51.509
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll grease and check the bearings on the GT2. Not an emergency but don't let it slip, that one. I'll take it myself.</v>

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:59.319
<v Tomasz Nowak>GT2, yeah. I thought you were going to say it was an urgent bearing job for a second.</v>

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.530
<v Sarah Okafor>No, no—grease and check. Not calling it a bearing failure.</v>

00:04:04.849 --> 00:04:10.449
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it. Sarah Okafor on the GT2 bearings, not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:20.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace Liu, can you chase the purchase order for the line 2 guard by Thursday? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:27.089
<v Grace Liu>Sorry, I can't take that one. I haven't got the capacity to own the purchase order chase.</v>

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:38.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Dave, can you take that instead—chase the purchase order for the line 2 guard by Thursday? Same priority: not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:40.769 --> 00:04:46.720
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll take it instead. I'll chase the purchase order for the line 2 guard by Thursday.</v>

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.029
<v Grace Liu>Thanks. Definitely with you rather than me, then.</v>

00:04:53.149 --> 00:04:55.250
<v David Whitfield>Yep. My glamorous procurement career continues.</v>

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.250
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll send the shift handover report round by Thursday as well. Normal priority for that.</v>

00:05:04.009 --> 00:05:06.810
<v Hannah Price>That's the report, rather than another handover meeting?</v>

00:05:07.279 --> 00:05:11.480
<v Fiona Doyle>Just the report going round, yeah. No extra meeting hiding in there.</v>

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Fiona has the shift handover report, by Thursday, normal priority.</v>

00:05:18.019 --> 00:05:22.220
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, I'll take vibration readings on the turbine one compressor tomorrow morning.</v>

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, you clipped out. Which compressor?</v>

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.279
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The turbine one compressor. I'll take the vibration readings tomorrow morning.</v>

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:37.209
<v Sarah Okafor>Heard it that time. Olumide Adeyemi, vibration readings on the turbine one compressor tomorrow morning. Agreed.</v>

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.680
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, that's me.</v>

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:47.750
<v Tomasz Nowak>And my blocker hasn't changed: can't get to the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit until production gives us a window.</v>

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Still blocked, not a fresh commitment for today.</v>

00:05:54.829 --> 00:06:00.430
<v Fiona Doyle>Still waiting on parts for the air dryer too. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:05.300
<v David Whitfield>So that's still the parts hold, not something that's ready to go?</v>

00:06:07.529 --> 00:06:11.730
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. Still blocked. No work to allocate on that while we're waiting.</v>

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:22.889
<v Fiona Doyle>And we were going to replace the belt on the Air Compressor 1, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it. It's off this list.</v>

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:26.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that belt replacement isn't part of today's agreed work.</v>

00:06:27.839 --> 00:06:34.490
<v Hannah Price>And the water booster is closed, just so the old handover doesn't make it look like another live one.</v>

00:06:35.779 --> 00:06:44.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. We've kept the completed bits separate. Only thing raised without an owner is the fire panel function test, and that stays no rush.</v>

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:52.050
<v David Whitfield>I'm clear on my two. The wrapper tomorrow, purchase order for the line 2 guard by Thursday.</v>

00:06:52.889 --> 00:06:57.089
<v Fiona Doyle>Same here. Boiler feed pump tomorrow at 9:30, report round by Thursday.</v>

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.769
<v Olumide Adeyemi>All clear. Teams only swallowed the useful bit of my update, as usual.</v>

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:08.350
<v Tomasz Nowak>Could hear every word about my flapjack, though. Funny that.</v>

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.089
<v Sarah Okafor>Perfect audio for the important issues. Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
